Fix unsoundness where the well-formedness check of a quantifier that Dafny splits into parts for its triggers, inside a lambda or another copy, assumed each part for every value while checking the next, and fix compiling against a library whose quantifiers Dafny split and joined again. Dafny now keeps just the quantifier as written, and the verifier makes the parts from it, so the existence check of a let-such-that expression also takes the parts of an existential in it for disjuncts, as a `:|` statement's does.
